{"type":"message","id":"d01444a9","parentId":"a1d25e6f","timestamp":"2026-05-20T03:35:07.028Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still error 1101. This is a Cloudflare Workers error. Let me check if the `/send` endpoint exists or if it needs a different HTTP method. Let me also try GET on the send endpoint to see what happens, or try different variations.\n\nActually, error 1101 in Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker threw an unhandled exception\". This could be due to the JSON body parsing failing or something similar. Let me try with a very simple JSON body.\n\nWait, maybe the issue is that the request body has special characters like `\\n` and the system is not handling them properly. Let me try with a simpler message first.\n\nOr maybe the issue is the Content-Type header. \n\nLet me test with a minimal payload to isolate whether this is a body parsing issue or something else with the endpoint itself.\n\nThe error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically indicates the worker itself is failing, possibly due to an unhandled exception in the Durable Object or storage layer. The message was working fine when fetched, so the database seems functional. I should try a simpler JSON structure without newlines to see if that's what's causing the worker to throw an exception during processing.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-30ad7d0c-a7fa-429b-b979-fbf089aef811","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try different content field names\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat test 03:30 UTC\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":21454,"output":342,"cacheRead":256,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22052,"cos